<p>The offensive line result is the most striking on this list. Linemen are the heaviest players on the field, and their 40 times typically change the least from year to year since size is prioritized over speed at the position. A record-setting average here suggests the shift toward faster, more athletic offensive linemen — players built to pull, climb to the second level, and handle zone-blocking schemes — is showing up in testing numbers league-wide, not just in a handful of standout prospects.</p>
